  "interpretation": "On the hold-out period the model correctly flagged 850 of 984 products that went on to stock out (recall 86.4%) and missed 134. Of everything it flagged as High Risk, 33.8% did stock out (1,665 false alarms), so about 2.0 unnecessary checks per real stockout caught. Accuracy is 69.3%, but only 16.8% of rows are actual stockouts, so accuracy alone is misleading: always answering 'Low Risk' would score 83.2% while catching nothing. ROC-AUC is 0.84 and PR-AUC is 0.46 (PR-AUC of a random scorer would be about 0.17). For comparison, the simple rule 'days of cover < lead time' reaches recall 80.1% and precision 31.0%. These figures come from synthetic data and say nothing about real-world performance.",
